/-!
# Restriction of line-bundle classes to dense open subschemes

Let `X` be a Noetherian integral scheme whose local rings are unique factorization domains (for
instance a regular scheme all of whose points have codimension at most two, such as a regular model
of a curve over a discrete valuation ring), and let `j : U ⟶ X` be an open immersion from a
nonempty scheme `U`. Under the Weil–Cartier Picard group isomorphism
`Cl(X) ≃+ Additive (LineBundleClass X)` of `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.CartierDivisor.Factorial`,
pullback of line-bundle classes along `j` corresponds to restriction of Weil divisors along the
injection of codimension-one points `CodimensionOnePoint U → CodimensionOnePoint X`.

Because `j` induces an isomorphism of function fields `K(X) ≅ K(U)`, every principal Weil divisor
on `U` extends to a principal Weil divisor on `X`. Consequently (Hartshorne, Proposition II.6.5;
Stacks Tag 0C9X):

1. Restriction `LineBundleClass.pullback j : LineBundleClass X → LineBundleClass U` is surjective.
2. A line-bundle class `a : LineBundleClass X` restricts to `1` on `U` if and only if `a` is an
   integer-power product of the prime-divisor line bundles `[𝒪_X(closure {η})]` supported at the
   finitely many codimension-one points `η` of `X` lying outside `Set.range j`.

When `R` is a discrete valuation ring with fraction field `K` and `toBase : X ⟶ Spec R` is a
regular Noetherian integral scheme of codimension at most two whose generic point lies outside the
special fibre, applying this to `genericFiberι R K toBase` (and to `Model.genericι`) shows that
restriction `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` is surjective with kernel generated by the irreducible components
of the special fibre.

## Main declarations

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap_vanishingIdeal_of_isOpenImmersion`: pulling back
  the vanishing ideal sheaf of a closed subset along an open immersion gives the vanishing ideal
  sheaf of its preimage;
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.CodimensionOnePoint.mapOfIsOpenImmersion`: the injection on
  codimension-one points induced by an open immersion;
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.pullback_classGroupAddEquivLineBundleClass`:
  compatibility of `Cl ≃+ Pic` with pullback along a nonempty open immersion;
* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.pullback_surjective_of_isOpenImmersion` and
  `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.pullback_eq_one_iff_of_isOpenImmersion`: surjectivity
  and kernel characterization of `Pic(X) → Pic(U)` on locally factorial Noetherian integral
  schemes, with regular codimension-at-most-two specializations
  `pullback_surjective_of_isRegular` and `pullback_eq_one_iff_of_isRegular`;
* `TauCeti.pullback_genericFiberι_surjective` and `TauCeti.pullback_genericFiberι_eq_one_iff`:
  surjectivity and vertical-component kernel of `Pic(X) → Pic(X_K)` over a discrete valuation ring,
  together with `TauCeti.Model.pullback_genericι_surjective` and
  `TauCeti.Model.pullback_genericι_eq_one_iff`.

## References

* [R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*][hartshorne1977], Proposition II.6.5.
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0C9X](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9X): restriction of
  invertible sheaves from a regular model to its generic fibre.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

